// 49a control — is a FIXED short-circuit set safe against ticket 15's collapse?
//
// A valve that keys on the fixed set `(:error, _) | :nothing` (shape C) is only
// sound where `:nothing` is still a distinguishable member of the subject. It is
// not, in one case ticket 15 measured: `option<atom>` normalises to bare `atom`,
// because `:nothing` IS an atom and 09's rule absorbs a singleton into the
// cofinite top. A valve over such a value would short-circuit on a legitimate
// success.
//
// Ticket 15 made that collapse "an error at the declaration" — decisions.md:297.
// If that refusal is real, the hazard cannot reach a valve, and shape C needs no
// new machinery to be safe. This probe is the check.
module Collapse

// Expected: refused at the declaration, before any valve is involved.
public option<atom> Lookup(int id)
Lookup(id) when id > 0  -> :found
Lookup(id) when id <= 0 -> :nothing
